      "updated": 1789750774783,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Html's Syntax :\n\n- Elements - > theres a hieararchy of elements that describe what each element \nrepresents for example an img element represents an image\nsyntax of normal els = <img> </img>\nsyntax of void Els = <input />\n\n-Attributes are features u can add to ur elements tag and change it in some \nway most common attribute is the \"class\" attribute which gives that specific elemnt\nan alias to refer to so ;\n\n<img class=\"Dog-Image\"></img>\n\n<img class=\"Cat-IMage\"></img>\n\nso based on the classNames u can reference these elements by their aliases so\nin ur css u could do smth like\n\n.Dog-Image \n{ width : 300px;\n} /* this references those elements with the className \"dog-Image!\"*/",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Html's Syntax :\n\n- Elements - > theres a hieararchy of elements that describe what each element \nrepresents for example an img element represents an image\nsyntax of normal els = <img> </img>\nsyntax of void Els = <input />\n\n-Attributes are features u can add to ur elements tag and change it in some \nway most common attribute is the \"class\" attribute which gives that specific elemnt\nan alias to refer to so ;\n\n<img class=\"Dog-Image\"></img>\n\n<img class=\"Cat-IMage\"></img>\n\nso based on the classNames u can reference these elements by their aliases so\nin ur css u could do smth like\n\n.Dog-Image \n{ width : 300px;\n} /* this references those elements with the className \"dog-Image!\"*/",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
