      "seed": 901865407,
      "version": 790,
      "versionNonce": 1751191185,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789750774783,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "so sum of int angles = 5(x) where x is sum of exterior angles;\nofcouse its a convex polygon as book doesnt cover concaves\n\nNi = 5(360) - > [Ni = 1800];\nfind:\n   Number of sides;\nApproach :\n    we know that Linear pairs = Ni + Ne;\n    so 1800 + 360 = linearPairs;\n    why LinearPairs cuz we know that each linear pair is\n    180degrees hence we can divide them by 180 and find the n of\n    linearpairs or exterior angles or interior angles or the sides of \n    the polygon;\n  algebraically : \n    2160 / 180 - > [n = 12];\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "so sum of int angles = 5(x) where x is sum of exterior angles;\nofcouse its a convex polygon as book doesnt cover concaves\n\nNi = 5(360) - > [Ni = 1800];\nfind:\n   Number of sides;\nApproach :\n    we know that Linear pairs = Ni + Ne;\n    so 1800 + 360 = linearPairs;\n    why LinearPairs cuz we know that each linear pair is\n    180degrees hence we can divide them by 180 and find the n of\n    linearpairs or exterior angles or interior angles or the sides of \n    the polygon;\n  algebraically : \n    2160 / 180 - > [n = 12];\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
