    {
      "id": "rUUpSRJhDeoCKTqB5Okqw",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2163.7743146972102,
      "y": -4683.34513149246,
      "width": 1066.99853515625,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b8h",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 324271744,
      "version": 910,
      "versionNonce": 680352127,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789750774784,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Summary :\n\n- triangles are congruent if their pair of vertices can be perfectly matched on to the \npairs of other triangles\n- triangles can be said to be congruent just by deducting about three parts BUT magnitude will \nalways be there so SSS,SAS,ASA these are the theorems(for now posed as postulates)\n-triangles when said to be congruent can tell us alot of info about parallelism and stuff!;\n-if two interior congruent segments add up together to make an external segment then the endpoint\nshared between them is the midpoint bEcause this Scenario is only possible when the \nexternal segment is divided into congruent segments (midpoint);",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Summary :\n\n- triangles are congruent if their pair of vertices can be perfectly matched on to the \npairs of other triangles\n- triangles can be said to be congruent just by deducting about three parts BUT magnitude will \nalways be there so SSS,SAS,ASA these are the theorems(for now posed as postulates)\n-triangles when said to be congruent can tell us alot of info about parallelism and stuff!;\n-if two interior congruent segments add up together to make an external segment then the endpoint\nshared between them is the midpoint bEcause this Scenario is only possible when the \nexternal segment is divided into congruent segments (midpoint);",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
